+
+## Approach
+
+**Pattern reference**: `src/tally/money.py` — cents as int, no floats.
+
+**Vital slice**: sign-aware parse + one shared money formatter used by every command that prints an expense amount.
+**Cut list**: no sign handling for `split`/bills; no "refund" label in output.
+
+Suggested design (agent may adjust if simpler):
+- `money.parse_amount(text, allow_negative=False)`: optional leading `-` (before or after `$`). Zero (`-0`, `-0.00`) never yields a valid expense. Default stays non-negative so `split`/bills are unchanged.
+- `models.new_expense` and `Expense.from_row` pass `allow_negative=True`; `Expense.__post_init__` rejects `amount == 0` only.
+- `money.to_plain` MUST handle negatives: `-1550 // 100` is `-16`, so `-1550` would print `-16.50`. Format with sign + `divmod(abs(cents), 100)`.
+- Add `money.format_dollars(cents)` -> `$1,234.56` / `-$15.50` and replace the inline `f"${x // 100:,}.{x % 100:02d}"` copies in `cli.py` (add, list, summary, top, and split/due too since the helper is identical for non-negatives).
+- `reports.largest`: "top" sorts by amount; refunds sort last. Keep that behavior.
+
+---
+
+## Edge Case Checklist
+
+- [ ] `-15.50` is not stored or shown as `-16.50` (floor division on negatives)
+- [ ] `argparse` passes `-15.00` as a positional (it should, since no option looks like a number) — confirm in a CLI test
+- [ ] `-$15.00`, `$-15.00`, `-1,200.00` parse; `--5`, `-`, `-abc` are rejected
+- [ ] Zero rejected: `0`, `0.00`, `-0`, `-0.00`
+- [ ] Existing positive-amount tests still pass unchanged
